<title>CANADA: CanOxy Pete spuds Nigeria offshore well.</title>
<headline>CanOxy Pete spuds Nigeria offshore well.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Occidental Petroleum Ltd said on Monday it spudded its Ejulebe East No. 1 well on oil mining lease 109, offshore Nigeria.</p>
<p>CanOxy said the well is located about 15 km offshore in 50 feet of water and is assessing the reserve potential of a fault block adjacent to the main Ejulebe fault block where two wells have been successfully drilled to date.</p>
<p>The well will test three primary horizons which successfully tested commercial quantities of oil in the two prior wells, CanOxy said.</p>
</text>
